# Headers for Cloudflare Pages (also works on Netlify — same format).
#
# 1) The browser must revalidate the HTML on every load instead of reusing a
#    stale cached copy. This guarantees every browser runs the current sync code
#    and complements the no-cache <meta> tags inside the HTML. The wallpaper
#    images themselves are served from Supabase, so this only affects page files.
# 2) Basic security headers (checklist item 21): no MIME sniffing, no
#    click-jacking via iframes, no leaking full referrer URLs, and the page
#    never needs camera/microphone/geolocation access.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# The gallery document itself must NEVER be served from a cache. "public,
# max-age=0, must-revalidate" still lets a cache store the page and hand it back,
# and Safari in particular is happy to reuse a stale copy — which is how a
# browser ends up running an old, broken build of the page while every other
# browser has the current one. "no-store" removes the ambiguity. It costs one
# full HTML transfer per visit; the icons and robots.txt below stay cacheable.
/
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-store
/wallpapers
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-store
/wallpapers.html
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-store

# robots.txt / sitemap.xml change rarely — let the CDN cache them for an hour.
/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/sitemap.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
